Migration does not end when a workload successfully starts running in Azure. Post-migration optimization ensures that the new environment is secure, performant, reliable, and cost-effective.

Optimization activities include:

* Right-sizing resources
* Reviewing storage configuration
* Optimizing networking
* Implementing autoscaling
* Reviewing security controls
* Configuring monitoring
* Removing unused resources
* Evaluating managed services

For example, a virtual machine initially provisioned with excess CPU and memory can be right-sized after actual workload utilization is measured.

A real-life use case is an enterprise reducing its Azure monthly expenditure after identifying overprovisioned resources following a large migration.

Post-migration optimization converts a successful migration into an efficient long-term cloud environment.
